From 9f20e0e291e34f40a4d60d9f73943d1a6629da86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:31:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not ask Google's DNS servers about google.com when a site
 cannot be found

A navigation that fails to resolve its hostname, a typo is enough, makes
NetErrorTabHelper start DnsProbeService. It runs two probes side by side: one
through the system resolver and one that resolves google.com against Google
Public DNS, 8.8.8.8 and 8.8.4.4, over plain UDP with secure DNS switched off.
So every DNS error told Google the user's address and that a lookup had just
failed, whatever the user had chosen for Secure DNS.

The only gate is embedder_support::kAlternateErrorPagesEnabled, registered
true. It is now registered false. With it off the helper marks the probe as
not run, and the error page still says the site's address could not be found.
The captive portal service reads the same pref; its detection is switched off
on Android (enable_captive_portal_detection).
---
 chrome/browser/net/profile_network_context_service.cc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/net/profile_network_context_service.cc b/chrome/browser/net/profile_network_context_service.cc
index 74900da833b..b9649434820 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/net/profile_network_context_service.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/net/profile_network_context_service.cc
@@ -648,8 +648,12 @@ void ProfileNetworkContextService::ConfigureNetworkContextParams(
 // static
 void ProfileNetworkContextService::RegisterProfilePrefs(
     user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable* registry) {
+  // Bare: off by default. On a DNS error it starts a probe that resolves
+  // google.com against Google Public DNS (8.8.8.8) over plain UDP, outside the
+  // user's Secure DNS setting. The error page still says the address could not
+  // be found; it only skips the extra diagnosis.
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(embedder_support::kAlternateErrorPagesEnabled,
-                                true);
+                                false);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kQuicAllowed, true);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kGloballyScopeHTTPAuthCacheEnabled,
                                 false);
